# ==============================================================================
# crwsync Monorepo Environment Configuration Quick Reference
# ==============================================================================
# crwsync is a multi-service monorepo. Each deployable service reads its own
# .env file located within its application directory:
#
#   1. Backend API (NestJS + Socket.IO + BullMQ):
#      apps/backend/.env.example  ->  apps/backend/.env
#
#   2. Authenticated Dashboard (Next.js App Router):
#      apps/frontend/dash/.env.example  ->  apps/frontend/dash/.env
#
#   3. Public Marketing Web Portal (Next.js App Router):
#      apps/frontend/web/.env.example  ->  apps/frontend/web/.env
#
#   4. Demo & Seed Script (Optional):
#      .env.demo.example  ->  .env.demo
#
# ==============================================================================
# Local Development Quick Start
# ==============================================================================
# 1. Start Postgres, Redis, and MinIO:
#      docker-compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d
#
# 2. Copy the example files:
#      cp apps/backend/.env.example apps/backend/.env
#      cp apps/frontend/dash/.env.example apps/frontend/dash/.env
#      cp apps/frontend/web/.env.example apps/frontend/web/.env
#
# 3. Generate Prisma client & run migrations:
#      pnpm --filter @crwsync/backend run prisma:generate
#      pnpm --filter @crwsync/backend run prisma:migrate:dev
#
# 4. (Optional) Seed realistic demo workspace & accounts:
#      pnpm seed
#
# 5. Start development servers:
#      pnpm dev
# ==============================================================================
